 times the previous term, so the common ratio is $r=6.$\n\n- Sequence III is not a geometric sequence. To see this, we can calculate the first $3$ terms of the sequence and then compute the ratios of consecutive terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1) & =1 \\\\ f(2) & =2\\cdot 1+3=5 \\\\ f(3) & =2\\cdot 5+3=13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the first two pairs of consecutive terms have different ratios:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{f(2)}{f(1)}=\\frac{5}{1} & =5 \\\\ \\frac{f(3)}{f(2)}=\\frac{13}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn conclusion, only sequence II is a geometric sequence." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120672 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186120673 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120672 #edb/ref 1061 17456 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120672 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b14c637b-1418-59f5-9ac3-37a07d6ad580" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120672 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186121034 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120673 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186120674 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120673 #edb/ref 1061 17458 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120673 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c7323a52-d0b1-55ea-81f4-41623766b9db" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120673 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186119805 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120674 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186120675 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120674 #edb/ref 1061 17460 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120674 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "fd939fe8-9699-5d8a-9dce-0e749d48075e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120674 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186119806 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120675 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186120748 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120675 #edb/ref 1061 17464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120675 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "fd740ffd-227c-5f9c-9418-4c54bf1616ff" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120675 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186119807 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120724 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186120725 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120724 #edb/ref 1061 17940 #edb/ref 17